{"node":{"id":"HP:0002017","label":"Nausea and vomiting","ic":2.959,"definition":"Nausea is a commonly encountered symptom that has been defined as an unpleasant painless subjective feeling that one will imminently vomit. Vomiting has been defined as the forceful expulsion of the contents of the stomach, duodenum, or jejunum through the oral cavity. While nausea and vomiting are often thought to exist on a temporal continuum, this is not always the case. There are situations when severe nausea may be present without emesis and less frequently, when emesis may be present without preceding nausea."},"diseases":[{"id":"MONDO:0008752","label":"Alexander disease","in_core":true,"edge":{"id":"e_e54dd618651e","source":"MONDO:0008752","target":"HP:0002017","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:58 · ORPHA:58","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/58","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.9,"snippet":"Alexander disease: Nausea and vomiting (frequency HP:0040281) [TAS]"},{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:58","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/58","confidence":0.9,"snippet":"Nausea and vomiting — Very frequent (99-80%)"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.9,"independent_sources":["Orphanet"],"level":"curated"},"confidence":0.9},{"id":"MONDO:0019148","label":"Wolman disease","in_core":true,"edge":{"id":"e_9ebd5d07f8c8","source":"MONDO:0019148","target":"HP:0002017","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:75233 · ORPHA:75233","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/75233","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.9,"snippet":"Wolman disease: Nausea and vomiting (frequency HP:0040281) [TAS]"},{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:75233","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/75233","confidence":0.9,"snippet":"Nausea and vomit